@startuml activity-prototyping-cycle
!include style.iuml
title How each prototype iteration was built (iterative prototyping, proposal §3.2)

start
:Phase 0: analyse the proposal, plan the
architecture and the phases, record decisions as ADRs;
repeat
  :Design refinement: requirements for this phase
  (traceability matrix), interface and data changes;
  :Development: backend, AI service, phone app,
  admin website;
  :Internal testing: unit, database and widget tests,
  then the quality gate for each changed part
  (format, lint, types, tests, coverage of 80 % or more,
  build, audit);
  if (Gate passes?) then (no)
    :Fix the code, or the test if the behaviour
    should change (and say why);
  else (yes)
    :Commit and push, and CI runs the same gate;
    :Evaluation: check on the emulator or phone,
    owner's review and requests;
    :Record what was done and found
    (development log, traceability matrix);
  endif
repeat while (More phases or owner requests?) is (yes)
->no;
:End-to-end workflows on the live system (Phase 16),
performance against the targets (Phase 17),
final audit (Phase 18);
stop
@enduml
